    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n1426" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀδμ-ής</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῆτος</span>,
			ὁ, ἡ, poet. for
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀδάματος</span>, (<i><span class="en">
			Hom.
		</span></i> only in <i><span class="en">
			Od.
		</span></i>), of maidens, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>unwedded</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παρθένος ἀδμής</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					6.109
				</span></i>
			,<i><span class="en">
				228
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀδμῆτας ἀδελφάς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>OC</u>
					1056
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> of
			animals, <i>unbroken</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡμίονοι . . ἀδμῆτες</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					4.637
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b> c. gen.,
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀδμᾶτες νούσων</span>
			<i>unsubdued by</i> . . , <i><span class="en">
				B.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				19
			</span></i>.</div>
